Public keys (minisign, *.pub) that releases of TitanOS must be signed with.

An update is installed only if the manifest of the release carries a valid
signature of one of the keys in this directory. An image without a key
installs no updates at all.

Two keys may lie here at the same time: that is how a key is replaced. A
release that adds the new key is signed with the old one; the next ones
are signed with the new one.

See docs/RELEASING.md in the repository.
